{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"halfround-scowlful-polyp","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\nThe tests/interfaces/contracts cohort contains audited comments or docstrings that obscure current behavior with repetition, obvious narration, duplicated explanation, or historical detail. The audit is pinned to `9e65567b79ffe872534c3c656ade7b34340d8192`.\n\n## Approach\nEdit explanatory text only in this directory/subsystem cohort. Condense it to current, non-obvious rationale and constraints; retain every file-specific preserve item and consumer contract below. Grouping adjacent files from one subsystem keeps the change reviewable in one session and permits one coherent verification pass without changing executable behavior.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_cli_help_writing_guidelines_jerboa.py:1-14` — Preserve scoped positive and negative wording checks. Consumer: comment-hygiene scan only; no exact-text consumer.\n- `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_completion_budget.py:1-23,58-65,82-93,139-140` — Preserve the formula, bounds, default-versus-explicit policy, and offline seam. Consumer: comment-hygiene scan only; no exact-text consumer.\n- `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_error_code_taxonomy_contract.py:1-22,41-46` — Preserve vocabulary closure and the import-order caveat. Consumer: comment-hygiene scan only; no exact-text consumer.\n- `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_llm_config_authoritative_binding.py:1-25` — Preserve compose-once, freeze, fail-fast, and secret-exclusion invariants; summarize without project chronology. Consumer: comment-hygiene scan only; no exact-text consumer.\n- `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_llmrunner_error_codes_f75f_heldout.py:1-16` — Preserve the type-d